────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/spawn -o now takes a quoted path, so -o "out/a b.md" do x saves to out/a b.md and the task is do x. fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test all pass, and the commit is titled Fixes #1213.

What changed
• -o and --system now read their values through one shared reader in a new file, src/commands_spawn_args.rs. It replaces the old inline rejoin that only --system had. It's included from commands_spawn.rs with #[path], so main.rs wasn't touched.
• A quote opens only at the start of a value. "..." and '...' both work, spaces inside the quotes are kept as typed, and text right after the closing quote joins the value ("a b".md → a b.md). An unquoted value is still one word, so don't.md still works.
• Refused before anything runs: a quote that's never closed (the message names the flag and what was typed), and an empty -o "". Before this change, the unclosed case still started a sub-agent on a wrong path ("out/a) and wrong task.
• Unchanged: a bare -o with nothing after it is still read as task text, and the task text after the flags is split exactly as before.
• Also changed, and stated in the commit:
  • --system now accepts single quotes and refuses an unclosed quote. Before, it printed usage, or used half a prompt when task words followed.
  • When -o names a directory, the suggested file name is now quoted if the path has a space, so the suggestion parses back to that path (tested).
• src/commands_spawn.rs went from 4629 to 4621 lines, under its size cap.
• The docs sentence from the previous fix ("The file name is one word…") is replaced. Every #1213 reference in the repo describes finished work.

Tests
• Four new tests list where every word of each example ends up. One drives handle_spawn itself and checks that an unclosed quote registers no task and creates no file.
• The "before" column in the commit table comes from reading the old code, not from running it.
• Recall control: I disabled the quote detection, marked it NEUTERED, and checked the marker count before running. Six tests went red by name, including two existing --system tests; after restoring it, all 191 spawn tests pass. My first attempt was void: the comment I inserted broke compilation, so no tests ran. I noticed only because no test output printed, and redid it.

Separate problem found: /spawn --parallel -o x.md … throws the -o value away with no message. No open issue covered it and this fix doesn't touch it, so I filed it as #1224. It's read from the code only; I didn't run it.

The per-word before/after table and the control result are in the commit body and in a comment on #1213.
